From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:30:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/57] Change history: tint the unsaved changed text inside
 the lines

Orange lines (changed and not saved) now also get a light orange
background on the changed text itself: the theme warning colour at
about 22 % alpha, drawn behind the glyphs and under the selection. A
changed line is compared word by word (letters/digits/_ runs, whitespace
runs, single other chars) with the saved line it replaces; only the
inserted or changed words are tinted. Whole new lines are tinted whole.
In a replaced block of unequal length each new line takes the most
similar old line after the previous one (blocks up to 16 lines; larger
ones pair by position). Deleted text is not shown. Saved (green)
changes are not tinted.

The word diff runs in the same background pass as the line marks, with
the same 50 ms deadline, and is kept or dropped with them by the
generation counter; while a result is pending the tint lags the typing
by the usual debounce. A range over a wrapped line covers each visual
row.

Settings > Change history > "Highlight changed text" (config key
highlight_changed_text, on by default); "Show changed lines" off also
turns the tint off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

